<title>MONGOLIA: Mongolia Jan-April copper production up 24.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Mongolia Jan-April copper production up 24.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ULAN BATOR 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolian copper concentrate production stood at 149,300 tonnes in January to April, up 24.3 percent from 120,100 tonnes in the same period last year, the State Statistical Bulletin said in a report seen on Friday.</p>
<p>Production in April alone was 37,300 tonnes, up from 30,500 tonnes in the month last year.</p>
<p>Despite the rise in production, exports of copper concentrate in the first four months of the year fell 12.25 percent to 133,900 tonnes from 152,600 tonnes a year ago.</p>
<p>The bulletin gave no explanation for the export decline.</p>
</text>
